                                "sense_id": "5f44002f-c0b1-3a16-ad70-79f9405fa76c",
                                "text": "There is no breeze, no slightest shift of air-particles; yet down the gorge comes this cloud,--a cloud unsensible except to nostrils,--eddying as if swirling around the edges of leaves, riding on the air as gently as the low, distant crooning of great, sleepy jungle doves."
